1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,478
Not every model belongs to a product.

2
00:00:02,538 --> 00:00:06,870
A showroom piece on your home page, a
material sample in a blog post, a

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:11,261
packaging render on an About page — those
live in the 3D Model Library.

4
00:00:12,471 --> 00:00:14,582
Open 3D Model Library from the nav.

5
00:00:14,642 --> 00:00:19,545
Each entry is a model file plus a name,
its own viewer settings, and a permanent

6
00:00:19,605 --> 00:00:21,530
Model ID you can paste anywhere.

7
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,475
Worth being clear on the difference.

8
00:00:24,535 --> 00:00:28,705
A product model is attached to a product
and drawn by the product block

9
00:00:28,765 --> 00:00:29,539
automatically.

10
00:00:29,599 --> 00:00:34,424
A library model is standalone — you place
it deliberately, by ID or by embed code.

11
00:00:34,484 --> 00:00:35,974
The same file can be both.

12
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:39,134
Uploading is a drop zone. Drag a .

13
00:00:39,194 --> 00:00:44,340
glb straight from your desktop onto it, or
click it to open a file chooser.

14
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:50,102
Same twenty megabyte ceiling, same glb and
gltf formats, same Shopify Files storage

15
00:00:50,162 --> 00:00:51,629
as the product screen.

16
00:00:52,489 --> 00:00:55,552
The zone highlights as you drag over it
and tells you to release.

17
00:00:56,162 --> 00:00:57,313
Drop, and it uploads.

18
00:00:57,373 --> 00:01:01,695
Note it also syncs your shop library
metafield straight afterwards, which is

19
00:01:01,755 --> 00:01:06,539
what makes the new Model ID resolvable on
the storefront without you touching Setup.

20
00:01:07,399 --> 00:01:11,107
And it appears in the list, newest first,
with its size and date.

21
00:01:11,817 --> 00:01:16,478
Choose from Files works here too — import
a model already in your Shopify Files into

22
00:01:16,538 --> 00:01:18,501
the library without re-uploading it.

23
00:01:19,361 --> 00:01:21,415
Search filters by name as you type.

24
00:01:21,475 --> 00:01:26,428
Sort gives you newest, oldest, name A to
Z, or largest first — largest first is the

25
00:01:26,488 --> 00:01:30,716
useful one when you're hunting for the
file that's slowing a page down.

26
00:01:31,576 --> 00:01:35,179
There's a grid view as well as the list,
toggled top right.

27
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:37,041
Same actions, more per screen.

28
00:01:37,901 --> 00:01:42,117
Every row has three copy buttons and
they're for three different jobs.

29
00:01:42,177 --> 00:01:46,332
ID copies the Model ID — that's what the
Any Model theme block wants.

30
00:01:46,392 --> 00:01:50,730
Embed copies a ready-made iframe snippet
for anywhere that accepts HTML.

31
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:55,067
URL copies the raw glb file address, for
when you need the file itself.

32
00:01:55,927 --> 00:01:59,005
Click ID, and it's on your clipboard with
a confirmation.

33
00:01:59,065 --> 00:02:03,299
Paste that into the theme block and the
model appears, complete with its saved

34
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:03,959
settings.

35
00:02:04,504 --> 00:02:09,001
For tidying up, tick the checkboxes — they
appear on hover — or use Select all.

36
00:02:09,061 --> 00:02:13,211
A blue bar tells you how many are selected
and gives you Delete selected.

37
00:02:14,071 --> 00:02:16,079
Deleting is safer than it sounds.

38
00:02:16,139 --> 00:02:21,093
It removes the library entry — the name,
the settings, the ID — but the glb file

39
00:02:21,153 --> 00:02:23,286
itself stays in your Shopify Files.

40
00:02:23,346 --> 00:02:26,858
You're not destroying an asset, and you
can re-import it.

41
00:02:27,718 --> 00:02:32,469
If you hit your plan limit, the drop zone
dims and a banner explains the arithmetic:

42
00:02:32,529 --> 00:02:37,223
how many models in the library, how many
product assignments, and the reminder that

43
00:02:37,283 --> 00:02:39,056
a file used in both counts once.

44
00:02:39,916 --> 00:02:41,590
Click any row to open the model.

45
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:45,927
This screen gets its own tutorial next,
because it's where sharing and embedding

46
00:02:45,987 --> 00:02:50,101
happens — but note it has the same viewer
settings you learned on the product

47
00:02:50,161 --> 00:02:52,323
screen, saved against this library entry.

48
00:02:53,183 --> 00:02:57,968
Next, the part that lets you put a model
literally anywhere — including outside

49
00:02:58,028 --> 00:02:58,628
Shopify.
